  "reason": "The current best (config_041, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. We have strong evidence that scgpt is a poor RNA encoder (0.520 vs 0.725), but pca_n2000—a fundamentally different linear method—has never been tested with this best architecture. Config_039 isolates the RNA encoder variable while holding all other settings at their empirically optimal values. This reduces uncertainty about whether scvi_n200's advantage is specific to deep generative encoding or whether a simpler linear projection could match/exceed it. If pca_n2000 performs comparably, it suggests the bottleneck is elsewhere (e.g., fusion or image encoder) and guides the remaining 3 experiments toward those dimensions. If it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 is locked in and we can exploit the remaining budget on finer architectural tweaks. This is the highest-information experiment given the sparse evidence on pca_n2000 in the best-architecture regime."
}

